### Sattadhar Textile — Khata (credit ledger) module
### VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client). Run top to bottom.
### Sign in first (steps 1–2), then paste the ids from steps 3–4.
###
### The whole point of this file is the last block: run steps 16–21 as STAFF
### and watch the shop-wide views come back 403 while the per-customer ones
### keep working.

@base = http://localhost:4000
@api = {{base}}/api/v1

### ─── 1. Login as ADMIN ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# @name adminLogin
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "admin", "password": "ChangeMe@123" }

###
@adminAccess = {{adminLogin.response.body.data.accessToken}}

### ─── 2. Login as STAFF ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
### kirti is seeded with `payment.record` and `ledger.view` both ON.
# @name staffLogin
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "kirti", "password": "Staff@123" }

###
@staffAccess = {{staffLogin.response.body.data.accessToken}}

### ─── 3. Find the seeded customers — copy two ids below ─────────────────
### "Vasant Silk House" carries a seeded opening balance of 12,500.
### "Rohan Traders" has a deliberately small 5,000 credit limit.
GET {{api}}/customers?pageSize=50
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccess}}

###
@customerId = <PASTE_VASANT_SILK_HOUSE_ID>
@smallLimitCustomerId = <PASTE_ROHAN_TRADERS_ID>

### ─── 4. Find a product with stock — copy the id below ──────────────────
GET {{api}}/products?pageSize=50
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccess}}

###
@productId = <PASTE_ANY_IN_STOCK_PRODUCT_ID>

### ─── 5. The opening balance is a real ledger entry ─────────────────────
### Expect one OPENING row whose balanceAfter equals customer.outstanding.
GET {{api}}/ledger/customer/{{customerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccess}}

### ─── 6. A CREDIT sale — this is what raises the khata ──────────────────
# @name creditBill
POST {{api}}/bills
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccess}}

{
  "billingMode": "GST",
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "paymentMode": "CREDIT",
  "items": [{ "productId": "{{productId}}", "qty": 2 }]
}

###
@billId = {{creditBill.response.body.data.id}}

### ─── 7. Confirm the sale wrote a CREDIT_SALE row ───────────────────────
### The newest entry should be type CREDIT_SALE, carry the bill number, and
### its balanceAfter should equal the customer's new outstanding.
GET {{api}}/ledger/customer/{{customerId}}?pageSize=5
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccess}}

### ─── 8. Partial payment ────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Watch `allocations`: the money lands on the OLDEST unpaid bill first.
POST {{api}}/ledger/payment
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccess}}

{
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "amount": 500,
  "paymentMode": "UPI",
  "note": "Part payment at the counter"
}

### ─── 9. Payment against one named bill ─────────────────────────────────
### refBillId jumps the queue; anything left over still flows to older bills.
POST {{api}}/ledger/payment
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccess}}

{
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "amount": 1000,
  "paymentMode": "CASH",
  "refBillId": "{{billId}}"
}

### ─── 10. The bill's own dueAmount moved too ────────────────────────────
### paymentStatus should now read PARTIAL (or PAID if fully covered).
GET {{api}}/bills/{{billId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccess}}

### ─── 11. The full statement, oldest first ──────────────────────────────
### `totals.debit − totals.credit` must equal `customer.outstanding`.
GET {{api}}/ledger/customer/{{customerId}}?sort=asc&pageSize=100
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccess}}

### ─── 12. Debit note — charges the customer more ────────────────────────
POST {{api}}/ledger/note
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccess}}

{
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "type": "DEBIT",
  "amount": 250,
  "reason": "Delivery charge recovered"
}

### ─── 13. Credit note — forgives part of the balance ────────────────────
POST {{api}}/ledger/note
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccess}}

{
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "type": "CREDIT",
  "amount": 250,
  "reason": "Waived as goodwill"
}

### ─── 14. A note with no reason is refused ──────────────────────────────
### Expect 400 VALIDATION_ERROR.
POST {{api}}/ledger/note
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccess}}

{ "customerId": "{{customerId}}", "type": "CREDIT", "amount": 100 }

### ─── 15. Shop-wide outstanding + ageing (ADMIN) ────────────────────────
GET {{api}}/ledger/outstanding
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccess}}

###
GET {{api}}/ledger/ageing
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccess}}

### ─── 16. Credit limit — a sale that does not fit is refused ────────────
### Rohan Traders' limit is 5,000. Expect 409 CREDIT_LIMIT_EXCEEDED, and
### note that NOTHING is written: no bill, no stock movement, no ledger row.
POST {{api}}/bills
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccess}}

{
  "billingMode": "GST",
  "customerId": "{{smallLimitCustomerId}}",
  "paymentMode": "CREDIT",
  "items": [{ "productId": "{{productId}}", "qty": 20 }]
}

### ─── 17. The owner may override deliberately ───────────────────────────
### Same request plus the flag. Expect 201. A STAFF token cannot do this —
### the service drops the flag for anyone who is not ADMIN.
POST {{api}}/bills
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccess}}

{
  "billingMode": "GST",
  "customerId": "{{smallLimitCustomerId}}",
  "paymentMode": "CREDIT",
  "overrideCreditLimit": true,
  "items": [{ "productId": "{{productId}}", "qty": 20 }]
}

### ─── 18. Payment reminder — a wa.me link, nothing sent ─────────────────
### Paste `whatsappUrl` into a browser to open WhatsApp with the message typed.
POST {{api}}/ledger/reminder/{{customerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccess}}

### ═══ STAFF — the boundary ══════════════════════════════════════════════

### ─── 19. STAFF may read ONE customer's khata ───────────────────────────
### Expect 200.
GET {{api}}/ledger/customer/{{customerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{staffAccess}}

### ─── 20. STAFF may take money at the counter ───────────────────────────
### Expect 201.
POST {{api}}/ledger/payment
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{staffAccess}}

{
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "amount": 100,
  "paymentMode": "CASH",
  "note": "Counter collection"
}

### ─── 21. STAFF may NOT see the shop's book ─────────────────────────────
### All three expect 403 FORBIDDEN with no payload — not a filtered list,
### not a zeroed total.
GET {{api}}/ledger/outstanding
Authorization: Bearer {{staffAccess}}

###
GET {{api}}/ledger/ageing
Authorization: Bearer {{staffAccess}}

###
POST {{api}}/ledger/note
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{staffAccess}}

{
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "type": "CREDIT",
  "amount": 1000,
  "reason": "Staff should not be able to do this"
}

### ─── 22. CHEQUE / CARD / CREDIT are not receipt modes ──────────────────
### Expect 400. A khata payment is money already settled.
POST {{api}}/ledger/payment
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{staffAccess}}

{ "customerId": "{{customerId}}", "amount": 500, "paymentMode": "CHEQUE" }
